                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Detected Prohibited C Function\" vulnerability in C++ refers to the use of insecure or unsafe C library functions in the code. These functions are often prone to buffer overflow attacks, format string vulnerabilities, integer overflow, etc. The use of these functions can lead to serious security issues such as code execution, denial of service, or information disclosure.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, there is no direct use of prohibited C functions. However, the comparison operation could potentially lead to logical errors or unexpected behavior if not properly handled.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this type of vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n- Avoid using unsafe C library functions. Instead, use safer alternatives provided by the C++ Standard Library.\n- Always validate and sanitize input data.\n- Use secure coding practices and follow the principle of least privilege.\n- Regularly update and patch your software to fix any known vulnerabilities.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe provided code snippet is a comparison operation and does not directly involve any prohibited C functions. However, to ensure the comparison operation is safe and correct, you can add additional checks or use safer comparison methods. Here is a possible fix:\n\n```cpp\nif (src > 0 && src == numCpuDevices) {\n    // Your code here\n}\n```\n\nIn this fix, we ensure that `src` is greater than zero before comparing it with `numCpuDevices`. This can prevent potential issues if `src` is negative.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet does not require any specific library dependencies to execute properly.\n\n## OWASP and CWE Links\n\n- [OWASP C++ Secure Coding Practices](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-676: Use of Potentially Dangerous Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/676.html)\n\nPlease note that these links are active and accessible to anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
